    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0836" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.21/470: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Philip</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-23T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1919, 1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your May 20, 4 p.m.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d729-f1"/> Strictly confidential.</p>
                <p>From Johnson.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d729-f2"/></p>
                <p>The President has instructed the Department to take up treaty with Senate
                    immediately. Mr. Polk has written Senators Lodge and Knox giving them present
                    situation in full and urging action.</p>
                <p>Mr. Lodge’s attitude appears to be favorable though one or two points remain to
                    be cleared up. Will keep you informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
